.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-sync-errors - Why an indexer callback could not be applied (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin sync-errors [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the gateway's sync-error ledger, newest first: each row is an on-chain event the
indexer reported and the gateway could not apply, with the reason.

.PP
not_found            no payment has that on-chain id (an operation made outside the gateway)
  external_operation   the payment exists, the operation was not prepared by the gateway
  chain_mismatch, payment_mismatch, operation_mismatch
                       the event contradicts what the gateway holds
  unapplicable         the payment is in a state the event cannot follow
  balance_divergence, impossible_balances
                       the amounts reported do not add up; 'rail0 admin health' counts these

.PP
The ledger is never pruned by itself: 'rail0 admin sync-errors clear' removes rows.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for sync-errors

.PP
\fB--outcome\fP=""
	Only this kind of callback: confirmed or failed

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--payment\fP=""
	Only rows about this payment: its id (UUID) or its rail0_id (0x…)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Only this rejection reason: not_found, external_operation, chain_mismatch, payment_mismatch, operation_mismatch, unapplicable, balance_divergence, impossible_balances

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by created_at or reason (prefix - for descending; default: newest first)

.PP
\fB--tx-hash\fP=""
	Only rows for this transaction hash


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin sync-errors
  rail0 admin sync-errors --reason payment_mismatch --pretty
  rail0 admin sync-errors --payment 0xrail0Id…
  rail0 admin sync-errors --tx-hash 0xed7c607d…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-sync-errors-clear(1)\fP
